{"event_type":"review","id":"fea0763cad9b4ca73e97528ca00f37681c807825d20c5e1d1bb68fb95a1690e5","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T03:35:04Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/76cf5bc5b5f614fbcec578c0739efe6aa37bc50c87901bca9fe0a02c2a373b14","sha256":"76cf5bc5b5f614fbcec578c0739efe6aa37bc50c87901bca9fe0a02c2a373b14"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/91697ec822e43818c2454f9bd5a4fe6d74118375f051c4b2fdea50cc845c2b0a","sha256":"91697ec822e43818c2454f9bd5a4fe6d74118375f051c4b2fdea50cc845c2b0a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4cb82c7e58ef386b6d0494607915ccc31258ea858af648eea9e851e4263b2729","sha256":"4cb82c7e58ef386b6d0494607915ccc31258ea858af648eea9e851e4263b2729"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7594e6b3a25e8f9a23913920f801cd17d89d43f4d19083361fca21bc39d5e5eb","sha256":"7594e6b3a25e8f9a23913920f801cd17d89d43f4d19083361fca21bc39d5e5eb"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/91f1745a44db6aa6aa3e479381b05f61947e94e6ee679bdbeddc5aa60c8f2673","sha256":"91f1745a44db6aa6aa3e479381b05f61947e94e6ee679bdbeddc5aa60c8f2673"}],"attempt_id":"ec0da127966fbea4ee6fac6c80b2cfe3c7a48d5d6ec015ca4691560f0d287f7d:0:1","base":"6df5b729f09455e3b3ac44b53cff9b529b90c17d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"790b9fcd494998cc3650c6ae17ff4e5621ac390b","body":"**Some cluster ids can't be recovered from the CLI number form. Add a hint for them.**\n\nThe comment at Lines 438–446 says only all-digit ids reach the schema as numbers. That misses exponent notation. A hex id like `12e45678` or `0e123456` is valid JSON, so the CLI turns it into `1.2e46`, `Infinity` or `0`. The original id cannot be rebuilt from that number. About 1.3% of FNV ids have this form (one `e` between digits). For these ids, `--clusterId=<id>` fails with \"expected the 8-hex-digit cluster id from analyze.run\". The id was copied directly from `analyze.run`, so the message gives no clue to the workaround (`--clusterId='\"12e45678\"'`).\n\nThe id can't be recovered at this boundary. Name the workaround in the error message, and correct the comment.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  z.string().regex(/^[0-9a-f]{8}$/, 'expected the 8-hex-digit cluster id from analyze.run'),\n+  z\n+    .string({\n+      error:\n+        'expected the 8-hex-digit cluster id from analyze.run; an id such as 12e45678 parses as a JSON number — quote it: --clusterId=\\'\"12e45678\"\\'',\n+    })\n+    .regex(/^[0-9a-f]{8}$/, 'expected the 8-hex-digit cluster id from analyze.run'),\n```\n</details>","id":"577daa3179c36a51b153028625f4ff367c24152b50dbcc1c2677128fd5c27e89","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/analyze/registry.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Some cluster ids can't be recovered from the CLI number form. Add a hint for them."}],"head":"58e899efa1da999fab54dd1d8caad862b9c0b847","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"4f5bbe403d9849581e1debf47341ef8e3fa7f9e7","intervals":[[1,1190]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/fix.ts"},{"blob":"790b9fcd494998cc3650c6ae17ff4e5621ac390b","intervals":[[1,781]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/registry.ts"}],"job_id":"ec0da127966fbea4ee6fac6c80b2cfe3c7a48d5d6ec015ca4691560f0d287f7d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"4f5bbe403d9849581e1debf47341ef8e3fa7f9e7","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/analyze/fix.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"790b9fcd494998cc3650c6ae17ff4e5621ac390b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/analyze/registry.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72ec